# Audio Editing Features

## 1. Core Waveform Editing

* Cut, copy, paste, and delete audio
* Trim the beginning or end of a clip
* Split audio clips
* Merge audio clips
* Crop selected regions
* Replace selected regions with silence
* Reverse audio
* Fade in
* Fade out
* Crossfade between clips
* Adjustable clip volume
* Waveform zoom
* Timeline navigation
* Sample-accurate selection
* Snap selection to markers or timeline positions
* Undo and redo history

The editor should use non-destructive editing. All edits should be stored as instructions while keeping the original audio file unchanged.

## 2. Audio Repair and Cleanup

* Noise reduction
* Background hum removal
* Click and pop removal
* De-esser
* Breath reduction
* Silence detection
* Voice isolation
* Echo reduction
* Reverb reduction
* Automatic speech cleanup
* Clipping repair
* DC offset removal

These features are especially useful for cleaning interviews, radio recordings, speeches, and archived audio.

## 3. Effects and Audio Processing

* Equalizer
* Compressor
* Limiter
* Noise gate
* Reverb
* Delay
* Chorus
* Flanger
* Distortion
* Stereo widening
* Bass control
* Treble control
* High-pass filter
* Low-pass filter
* Effects chain
* Effect presets

Effects should support:

* Per-clip processing
* Master-output processing
* Real-time preview
* Effect bypass
* Before-and-after comparison
* Adjustable effect parameters
* Saving custom presets

## 4. Volume and Loudness Tools

* Peak normalization
* Loudness normalization
* Gain adjustment
* Automatic volume leveling
* Loudness meter
* Peak meter
* RMS meter
* True-peak meter
* Clipping indicators
* LUFS measurement
* Waveform clipping detection
* Broadcast loudness presets
* Podcast loudness presets
* Streaming loudness presets
* Music-mastering presets

These tools help ensure that audio remains clear, balanced, and consistent across different listening platforms.

## 5. Time and Pitch Editing

* Playback-speed adjustment
* Time stretching without changing pitch
* Pitch shifting without changing duration
* Tempo detection
* Beat-grid generation
* BPM adjustment
* Key detection
* Audio quantization
* Transient detection
* Automatic beat alignment

These features are useful for adjusting timing, correcting pitch, preparing clips, and aligning audio elements.
